          "text": "Clinical Indication:\nHistory of focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at age 33, currently occurring approximately once per year. Genetic etiology attributed to a pathogenic DEPDC5 variant, c.4396C>T. Seizures are drug responsive. Current antiseizure medications are brivaracetam and topiramate.\n\nTechnique:\nRoutine scalp EEG recording was performed using standard electrode placement and digital acquisition.\n\nFindings:\nNo waveform-level EEG findings were provided for interpretation. Accordingly, background organization and the presence or absence of interictal epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures cannot be assessed.\n\nImpression:\nIndeterminate routine EEG because waveform-level findings are unavailable. The clinical history of focal epilepsy and focal impaired-awareness seizures is not independently established or localized by this EEG report.",
